# 2026-09-18 workspace discipline (AGENTS.md §1/§2/§3): the DSH reference copy
# (read-only, never committed) and the test-instance checkout (nested git repo)
# are dev-private; tests/dsh-homes/ holds DSH_HOME state — disposable by
# design, only the .gitkeep marker is tracked.
references/
tests/deepseek-harness/
tests/dsh-homes/*
!tests/dsh-homes/.gitkeep
# WP-0.6 e2e artifacts
e2e/__screenshots__/
playwright-report/
test-results/
# pnpm pack output (scripts/e2e-run.sh packs on demand)
dsh-research-control-*.tgz
.npm-cache-tmp/
# WP-8.4 (SI-001) → publish revision: the release snapshot (8 root docs +
# schema/ + SNAPSHOT.md) IS COMMITTED to the version tree — a git install
# (host publish.md "build-script catch") fetches sources only, so the frozen
# surface must ship with the tree or the package fail-louds at boot
# (src #resolveSchemaRoot). The workspace root keeps the authoring canonical;
# `pnpm run build` (scripts/snapshot-release.mjs) re-copies it and sha256-asserts
# identity, so the committed copy cannot drift. lib/ is ALSO committed
# prebuilt (V2 release revision): pnpm >= 10 refuses to run dependency build
# scripts unless the user grants allowBuilds in their own pnpm-workspace.yaml,
# and a git install (`dsh plugin add github:...` / file checkout) must work
# out of the box — so the runnable surface ships with the tree and the
# install-time `prepare` build script was dropped. Release discipline:
# `pnpm run build` BEFORE every push/pack; `pack:verify` asserts the lib
# surface after packing.

